#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:141
msgid "``uv run --script script.py``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:144
msgid "Only in pipx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:146
msgid ""
"``pipx inject`` / ``uninject`` add or remove a package in place. ``uv tool "
"install --with`` reaches the same end state by rebuilding the venv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:148
msgid ""
"``pipx runpip <venv> install ...`` runs pip against a tool's venv, or ``uv "
"pip`` under the uv backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:149
msgid ""
"``--include-deps`` exposes entry points from every dependency. uv requires "
"you to enumerate dep packages with ``--with-executables-from``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:151
msgid "``--suffix`` keeps two copies of the same tool side-by-side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:152
msgid ""
"``--global`` and the ``PIPX_GLOBAL_*`` variables drive a system-wide install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:153
msgid "Manual pages get symlinked under ``$PIPX_MAN_DIR``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:154
msgid ""
"``pipx manifest sync <manifest>`` applies an explicit desired set; ``pipx "
"manifest lock <manifest>`` writes one PEP 751 lock per selected tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:156
msgid ""
"``pipx install-all <spec.json>`` rebuilds every venv from a ``pipx list --"
"output json`` snapshot for cross-machine migration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:158
msgid ""
"``[project.entry-points.\"pipx.run\"]`` declares pipx-specific runtime "
"extras in the package metadata."
msgstr ""
"``[project.entry-points.\"pipx.run\"]`` 會在軟體包中繼資料中宣告 pipx 專用的"
"執行時額外項目。"

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:159
msgid ""
"``pipx environment`` prints every variable and its resolved value in one "
"place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:160
msgid ""
"``--cooldown DAYS`` provides the same release-age policy through pip and uv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:163
msgid "Only in uv tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:165
msgid ""
"``uv tool list`` toggles columns via ``--show-with``, ``--show-paths``, ``--"
"show-version-specifiers``, ``--show-extras``, ``--show-python``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:167
msgid "``uvx --with-editable PATH`` adds editable extras for a one-off run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:168
msgid ""
"``uv tool upgrade --all -p 3.13`` re-pins every tool to a different Python "
"in one shot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:169
msgid ""
"``uv python install/list/find/pin/upgrade/uninstall`` integrates managed "
"Python; uv auto-fetches when the requested Python isn't installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:171
msgid ""
"``--torch-backend`` and ``--isolated`` add controls that pipx does not "
"expose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:172
msgid ""
"The content-addressed cache spans ``uv pip``, ``uv tool``, ``uv run``, and "
"``uv venv``. Wheels downloaded once get reused everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:176
msgid "Gotchas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:178
msgid ""
"``uvx`` reuses cached envs across invocations until you prune the cache "
"(``uv cache clean``), pin a new version (``uvx black@latest``), or pass ``--"
"refresh``. ``pipx run`` caches for 14 days and accepts ``--refresh`` for an "
"early replacement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:181
msgid ""
"``uvx`` prefers a persistent install when one exists. After ``uv tool "
"install ruff``, plain ``uvx ruff`` reuses that env instead of building an "
"ephemeral one. Pass ``--isolated`` to bypass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:183
msgid ""
"``uv tool`` ignores project-local ``.python-version`` files. ``uv run`` "
"honors them; tool envs do not. pipx never reads them; pass ``--python`` or "
"set ``PIPX_DEFAULT_PYTHON``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:185
msgid ""
"``uv python upgrade`` only bumps patch versions. To move a tool from 3.12 to "
"3.13 run ``uv tool upgrade --all -p 3.13``. pipx's equivalent is ``reinstall-"
"all --python python3.13``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:187
msgid ""
"``uv run --script`` needs a real on-disk path. When ``pipx run script.py`` "
"content arrives via URL or named pipe, the uv backend falls back to building "
"a venv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:191
msgid "Picking one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:193
msgid ""
"pipx wins when you need its tool-specific extras: ``inject``/``uninject``, "
"``--global``, ``--suffix``, manual pages, or ``pipx install-all`` for "
"migration. Install ``pipx[uv]`` to keep that surface and pick up uv-speed "
"venv creation. Reach for ``uv tool`` when you already drive uv for managed "
"Python or ``uv run --script`` and want one binary for everything. Running "
"both is fine; the only collision point is the shared bin dir, and both sides "
"refuse to overwrite without ``--force``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:201
msgid "pipx vs poetry and pipenv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:203
msgid ""
"pipx is used solely for application consumption: you install CLI apps with "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:204
msgid ""
"pipenv and poetry are CLI apps used to develop applications and libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:205
msgid ""
"All three tools wrap pip and virtual environments for more convenient "
"workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:207
msgid ""
"Example: install poetry with pipx, ``pipx install poetry``; run poetry "
"without installing it, ``pipx run poetry --help``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:212
msgid "pipx vs venv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:214
msgid "venv is part of Python's standard library in Python 3.2 and above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:215
msgid ""
"venv creates \"virtual environments\", which are sandboxed Python "
"installations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:216
msgid "Under the pip backend, pipx relies heavily on the venv package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:218
msgid ""
"Example: pipx installs packages into environments created with venv, ``pipx "
"install black --backend pip --verbose``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:222
msgid "pipx vs pyenv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:224
msgid ""
"pyenv manages Python versions on your system. It helps you install versions "
"like Python 3.11, 3.12, and so on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:225
msgid ""
"pipx installs packages in virtual environments and exposes their entry "
"points on your ``PATH``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:227
msgid ""
"Example: install a Python interpreter with pyenv, then install a package "
"with pipx using that interpreter, ``pipx install black --python=python3.11`` "
"where ``python3.11`` was installed by pyenv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:232
msgid "pipx vs pipsi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:234
msgid "pipx and pipsi both install packages in a similar way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:235
msgid "pipx is under active development; pipsi is no longer maintained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:236
msgid ""
"pipx keeps its shared pip upgraded, refreshing it every 30 days under the "
"pip backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:237
msgid ""
"pipx can run an app in one line, leaving your system unchanged after it "
"finishes (``pipx run APP``); pipsi cannot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:238
msgid "pipx can recursively install binaries from dependent packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:239
msgid ""
"pipx has more CLI options such as ``upgrade-all``, ``reinstall-all``, and "
"``uninstall-all``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:240
msgid ""
"pipx is more modern. It requires Python 3.11+ and, under the pip backend, "
"uses the standard-library ``venv`` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:241
msgid "pipx works with Python homebrew installations while pipsi does not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:242
msgid "pipx lets you see each command it runs by passing ``--verbose``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:245
msgid "Migrating to pipx from pipsi"
msgstr "從 pipsi 遷移至 pipx"

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:247
msgid ""
"After you have installed pipx, run `migrate_pipsi_to_pipx.py <https://raw."
"githubusercontent.com/pypa/pipx/main/scripts/migrate_pipsi_to_pipx.py>`_. "
"You can do this with pipx itself:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:250
msgid ""
"$ pipx run https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pypa/pipx/main/scripts/"
"migrate_pipsi_to_pipx.py"
msgstr ""
"$ pipx run https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pypa/pipx/main/scripts/"
"migrate_pipsi_to_pipx.py"

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:256
msgid "pipx vs brew"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:258
msgid "Both brew and pipx install CLI tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:259
msgid ""
"They install from different sources: brew uses a curated repository specific "
"to brew, and pipx generally uses PyPI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:261
msgid ""
"Example: brew can install pipx, but the two generally do not interact much."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:265
msgid "pipx vs npx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:267
msgid ""
"Both can run CLI tools. npx searches ``node_modules`` and otherwise runs in "
"a temporary environment; ``pipx run`` searches ``__pypackages__`` and "
"otherwise runs in a temporary environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:269
msgid "npx works with JavaScript and pipx works with Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:270
msgid ""
"Both make running executables written in a dynamic language as easy as "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:271
msgid "pipx can also install tools globally; npx cannot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:273
msgid "Example: none. These tools work for different languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:277
msgid "pipx vs pip-run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:279
msgid ""
"`pip-run <https://github.com/jaraco/pip-run>`_ is focused on running "
"**arbitrary Python code in ephemeral environments**, while pipx is focused "
"on running **Python binaries in ephemeral and non-ephemeral environments**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:282
msgid ""
"For example, these two commands both install poetry to an ephemeral "
"environment and invoke poetry with ``--help``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:284
msgid ""
"pipx run poetry --help\n"
"pip-run poetry -- -m poetry --help"
msgstr ""
"pipx run poetry --help\n"
"pip-run poetry -- -m poetry --help"

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:291
msgid "pipx vs fades"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:293
msgid ""
"`fades <https://github.com/PyAr/fades>`_ runs **individual** Python scripts "
"inside automatically provisioned virtualenvs with their dependencies "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:296
msgid ""
"Both `fades <https://github.com/PyAr/fades#how-to-mark-the-dependencies-to-"
"be-installed>`_ and :doc:`pipx run <../reference/examples>` let you specify "
"a script's dependencies in specially formatted comments, but the exact "
"syntax differs. pipx's syntax is standardized by a `provisional "
"specification <https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/inline-"
"script-metadata/>`_; fades's syntax is not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:300
msgid ""
"Both tools automatically set up reusable virtualenvs containing the "
"necessary dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:301
msgid ""
"Both can download Python scripts or packages to execute from remote "
"resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:302
msgid ""
"fades can only run individual script files while pipx can also run packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:306
msgid "pipx vs pae/pactivate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:308
msgid ""
"*pae* is a Bash command-line function distributed with `pactivate <https://"
"github.com/cynic-net/pactivate>`_ that uses pactivate to create non-"
"ephemeral environments focused on general use, rather than just running "
"command-line applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:312
msgid ""
"There is a `detailed comparison <https://github.com/cynic-net/pactivate/blob/"
"main/doc/vs-pipx.md>`_, but to summarize:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:314
msgid "Similarities:"
msgstr "相似之處："

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:316
msgid ""
"Both create isolated environments without having to specify (and remember) a "
"directory in which to store them."
msgstr "兩者都會建立隔離環境，無須指定（並記住）存放環境的目錄。"

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:317
msgid ""
"Both let you use any Python interpreter available on your system (subject to "
"the version restrictions below)."
msgstr ""
"兩者都能讓您使用系統上可用的任何 Python 直譯器（但須符合以下版本限制）。"

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:319
msgid "pae advantages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:321
msgid ""
"Supports all versions of Python from 2.7 upward. pipx requires 3.11 or above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:322
msgid "Fewer dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:323
msgid ""
"Easier to have multiple versions of a single program, or use different "
"Python versions for one program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:324
msgid ""
"Somewhat more convenient for running arbitrary command-line programs in "
"virtual environments, installing multiple packages in a single environment, "
"and activating virtual environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:326
msgid ""
"Integrates well with source repos using `pactivate <https://github.com/cynic-"
"net/pactivate>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:328
msgid "pae disadvantages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:330
msgid "Usable with the Bash shell only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:331
msgid ""
"Slightly less quick and convenient for installing or running command-line "
"programs from single Python packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:332
msgid "Can be slower than pipx at creating virtual environments."
msgstr ""
